[8.000, "o", "  sufficiency gate: the evidence does NOT support a cause (8.0s); missing: A GA4 sessions-by-medium breakdown for June that actually returns rows (the query run returned 0 rows), to check whether paid-search traffic itself dropped around June 14-15; Statistical confirmation that the June 15 level shift is real rather than an artifact of the asymmetric window (the tool explicitly could not establish it); A dated marketing/ads platform record (e.g. Google Ads spend or click data) showing the campaign pause and its magnitude, to connect 'ads paused' with the size of the signup drop; Any signup funnel or product-side check ruling out a concurrent app/site issue, since feature flag and commit searches were all empty rather than confirmatory\r\n"]
